					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/themightymcb" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4483018); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4483018&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606100941" alt="TheMightyMcB" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4483018)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/themightymcb" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4483018); return false;" >TheMightyMcB</a></span> <span class="odate time_1559180628 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">30 May 2019 01:43</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4265784">
									

<p>Yet again I bamboozled the bread with promises of crit. No matter. Crit waits for no man.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Minor&nbsp;Gripes</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Minor&nbsp;Gripes</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-4966 is to be kept within a modified humanoid containment cell sized appropriately for a domestic cat to move freely.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>To be honest, I don't really think the domestic cat bit is necessary. Surely if a humanoid could live semi-comfortably, so could a house cat, no?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>This cell is furnished with</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Should be &quot;is to be furnished with&quot;.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Balaenoptera musculus<sup>1</sup></p>
</blockquote>
<p>I personally prefer using parentheses for common names next to the scientific name, but meh maybe that's just me. This is where I pick nits, after all.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The only physical traits of SCP-4966 unable to be altered are it’s existing facial features and gray coloration.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Maybe should be &quot;[&#8230;] traits of SCP-4966 <strong>that are</strong> unable to be altered [&#8230;]&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>An adult male <em>Crotalus horridus</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p>Oh hey one of my skips references timber rattlesnakes too! That's kinda cool!</p>
<blockquote>
<p>an anal fin</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This begs the question: Does Tubbioca have an anus? How can one have an anal fin with no anus? /s of course</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Alces alces Americana</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why is it that random ass skips end up explaining people's usernames to me? Did it for procy twice and now for alces. Funny how that works.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>a raid on Site-██</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Bluh, nitpick but I always preferred a number over site blackbox myself.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I’m not a organ psychic</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Not sure if this is a quirk of Tubbioca speak or if this was a typo, so I'm just gonna point it out.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>For its role in discovering the informants, SCP-4966 was provided a bag of Tostitos brand tortilla chips.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is fantastic. Better than even the Foundation Pat on the Back Award, I think.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>This was just a fun and cute article, and it was great. The development of the mannerisms of the plushie combined with that interview at the end and the foiling of a dastardly CI plot made for an interesting ride from start to finish.</p>
<p>Take my +1, and my apologies for not being able to crit this before posting.</p>

							</div>

								
					
